WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.368
Welcome to the ANC Hub.

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:07.212
This is the starting point for the team:
useful resources, shared updates,

00:00:07.212 --> 00:00:10.442
connected channels, and pages you can
build yourself.

00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:12.864
This walkthrough shows the owner account.

00:00:12.864 --> 00:00:16.900
Other people see the sections and controls
their permissions allow.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.744
We will start with everyday work, then
finish with activity and access.

00:00:22.544 --> 00:00:25.380
The resource library keeps the main tools
close.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.280
Search by a name or topic, or use the
category buttons.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.825
The bookmark saves a resource to your own
Saved view.

00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:35.307
Open resource takes you to the
destination.

00:00:35.307 --> 00:00:40.270
The small arrow expands the details right
here: a summary, category, and who can

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:40.979
see it.

00:00:40.979 --> 00:00:44.879
Admins can edit or archive a card from
this same area.

00:00:45.679 --> 00:00:49.782
Choose Add resource to start with a link
or a short description.

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:53.200
Switch to Page when you want an editable
workspace instead.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.935
The suggested prompts give you a starting
point.

00:00:55.935 --> 00:01:00.722
Open Prompt library to browse more ideas,
then choose one and change the wording

00:01:00.722 --> 00:01:02.089
to fit your task.

00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:05.166
Nothing is submitted until you choose the
create button.

00:01:05.966 --> 00:01:10.336
After the assistant prepares a resource,
review the name, description, and

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:10.733
destination.

00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:13.514
Set the category and audience before
saving.

00:01:13.514 --> 00:01:18.678
The cover is generated from the resource
name in a consistent ANC style.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:23.842
Choose ANC Blue, Midnight, or Ice,
regenerate it, or upload your own image.

00:01:23.842 --> 00:01:25.430
The summary remains editable.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:30.992
This review step is where you check the
details the team will actually see.

00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:34.491
Explore with AI opens a research
workspace.

00:01:34.491 --> 00:01:37.576
Ask a specific question and start the
search.

00:01:37.576 --> 00:01:42.204
The progress panel shows what is happening
while the answer is prepared.

00:01:42.204 --> 00:01:46.446
The brief includes numbered references,
with the source links beside it.

00:01:46.446 --> 00:01:49.531
Open a source to check its full context.

00:01:49.531 --> 00:01:54.544
Save to library carries a useful result
into the resource form for review.

00:01:55.344 --> 00:02:00.372
The Assistant button opens the side panel,
so you can keep working in the Hub.

00:02:00.372 --> 00:02:05.064
Type a rough request, then use Improve,
the magic wand, to make it clearer

00:02:05.064 --> 00:02:05.734
before sending.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:10.092
The improved wording stays in the box and
you can still edit it.

00:02:10.092 --> 00:02:11.767
Undo restores your original words.

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:15.119
Create builds a page; Research looks for a
sourced answer.

00:02:15.919 --> 00:02:18.793
Here we ask for a venue site visit
checklist.

00:02:18.793 --> 00:02:23.264
The assistant prepares an actual editable
draft, then returns a card with a link

00:02:23.264 --> 00:02:26.139
to open it and a control to edit it.

00:02:26.139 --> 00:02:28.374
Watch the progress stages while it works.

00:02:28.374 --> 00:02:30.291
Stop is available during a request.

00:02:30.291 --> 00:02:34.123
Pages start with restricted access, so
creating a draft does not immediately

00:02:34.123 --> 00:02:35.720
share it with the team.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.462
History shows your saved conversations.

00:02:38.462 --> 00:02:41.959
Search for a chat and reopen it to
continue.

00:02:41.959 --> 00:02:45.067
Back returns from history to the current
conversation.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.398
New chat starts a separate thread.

00:02:47.398 --> 00:02:51.283
Close, or Escape, hides the assistant
without deleting the conversation.

00:02:51.283 --> 00:02:53.614
Reopen it from the Assistant button.

00:02:53.614 --> 00:02:57.888
A request already running can continue
while the panel is closed.

00:02:58.688 --> 00:03:02.488
Open and edit the new page to work
directly in its content.

00:03:02.488 --> 00:03:05.654
Change the title or introduction, then
click into the body.

00:03:05.654 --> 00:03:10.087
Type a slash to choose a block, such as a
heading, list, or checklist.

00:03:10.087 --> 00:03:14.520
Type an at sign to mention a person or
insert an available app widget.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.636
The widget gives the page a useful
destination without making you build a

00:03:18.636 --> 00:03:19.586
separate card layout.

00:03:20.386 --> 00:03:24.734
Select text to reveal the editing toolbar,
then choose Edit with AI.

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:30.169
Give a direct instruction, such as make
this shorter and turn it into an action

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:30.532
checklist.

00:03:30.532 --> 00:03:35.967
The assistant uses the selected text and
the page context it is allowed to read.

00:03:35.967 --> 00:03:38.503
Review the suggested result before
applying it.

00:03:38.503 --> 00:03:42.851
You can improve part of a page without
rebuilding the whole thing.

00:03:43.651 --> 00:03:47.231
Preview shows the page as a reader will
see it.

00:03:47.231 --> 00:03:50.453
Save draft keeps the current version for
further editing.

00:03:50.453 --> 00:03:53.675
In Page settings, choose the audience
before you publish.

00:03:53.675 --> 00:03:57.255
Selected people, admins, and Ahmad only
are different access choices.

00:03:57.255 --> 00:03:59.761
The standalone link follows those same
rules.

00:03:59.761 --> 00:04:04.058
Mentioning someone does not grant access,
and an app widget keeps the

00:04:04.058 --> 00:04:05.490
destination app’s own permissions.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:11.721
Saved pages appear below the main Hub tabs
and as page cards in the library.

00:04:11.721 --> 00:04:15.342
The Team apps page collects available
tools in one place.

00:04:15.342 --> 00:04:19.326
The assistant can also prepare a people
directory from connected profiles.

00:04:19.326 --> 00:04:23.309
It uses available details and images;
missing information should remain missing.

00:04:23.309 --> 00:04:27.292
The page and its app widgets still respect
the viewer’s access.

00:04:28.092 --> 00:04:32.742
For a usage report, ask which app and
period you want to review.

00:04:32.742 --> 00:04:35.246
Report options let you choose them
explicitly.

00:04:35.246 --> 00:04:39.539
The resulting page shows the measurement
period, key figures, daily charts, and

00:04:39.539 --> 00:04:40.254
supporting breakdowns.

00:04:40.254 --> 00:04:44.189
The report’s figures come from the
connected analytics, while the surrounding

00:04:44.189 --> 00:04:45.620
findings can be edited.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.766
Private analytics remain restricted to
Ahmad.

00:04:47.766 --> 00:04:50.270
Figures are concealed in this training
recording.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:54.101
Team timeline is the shared conversation
space.

00:04:54.101 --> 00:04:59.296
Choose an Update, Question, or Team win,
write your message, and optionally

00:04:59.296 --> 00:05:00.595
attach a resource.

00:05:00.595 --> 00:05:05.790
Existing posts support likes and comments,
while admins can pin or moderate

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:06.223
them.

00:05:06.223 --> 00:05:09.254
Use the filters to focus the feed.

00:05:09.254 --> 00:05:11.851
This composer example is left unpublished.

00:05:11.851 --> 00:05:17.480
The timeline is for team conversations;
activity records live in a separate tab.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:21.391
Slack channels brings your available
channels into one view.

00:05:21.391 --> 00:05:26.922
Search for a channel, select it to read
recent updates, and use Open in Slack to

00:05:26.922 --> 00:05:28.305
continue the conversation there.

00:05:28.305 --> 00:05:31.762
Channel access follows the signed-in
person’s verified Slack identity and

00:05:31.762 --> 00:05:32.107
membership.

00:05:32.107 --> 00:05:35.910
Being a Hub admin does not unlock somebody
else’s private channels.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:39.021
We are keeping message contents out of
this recording.

00:05:39.821 --> 00:05:44.748
Team activity answers who did what, where,
and when, for the actions the

00:05:44.748 --> 00:05:45.885
connected systems record.

00:05:45.885 --> 00:05:50.811
Filter by person, app, or time period, and
search for a specific action.

00:05:50.811 --> 00:05:55.738
Entries show a timestamp, source, and
identity information, with a link to the

00:05:55.738 --> 00:05:56.875
item when available.

00:05:56.875 --> 00:06:01.801
Check the coverage details: this is
recorded activity, not a claim that every

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:03.317
action everywhere is captured.

00:06:03.317 --> 00:06:05.212
Private details are concealed here.

00:06:06.012 --> 00:06:09.032
Team and access brings the rules together.

00:06:09.032 --> 00:06:14.209
Hub tabs controls the main sections;
Sidebar tabs controls the wider
navigation.

00:06:14.209 --> 00:06:19.386
App widgets manages the app catalog, and
Team roles separates owners, admins,

00:06:19.386 --> 00:06:20.249
and members.

00:06:20.249 --> 00:06:24.994
AI access lets Ahmad decide which
capabilities and connected sources other

00:06:24.994 --> 00:06:26.289
admins can use.

00:06:26.289 --> 00:06:28.446
Some capabilities remain Ahmad only.

00:06:28.446 --> 00:06:33.623
These controls set the boundaries the
assistant follows when it creates or

00:06:33.623 --> 00:06:34.486
retrieves content.

00:06:35.286 --> 00:06:41.095
Ahmad can open View as user, find an
account, and enter that person’s actual
Hub

00:06:41.095 --> 00:06:41.482
experience.

00:06:41.482 --> 00:06:44.193
Here we use the dedicated verification
account.

00:06:44.193 --> 00:06:49.228
The banner makes the active identity clear
and provides Return to my account.

00:06:49.228 --> 00:06:54.263
This is a real working session: changes
affect that account and are audited

00:06:54.263 --> 00:06:55.037
under Ahmad.

00:06:55.037 --> 00:06:59.298
Use it to check permissions and workflows,
then return when finished.

00:06:59.298 --> 00:07:02.009
Linked apps still manage their own sign-
in.

00:07:02.809 --> 00:07:08.786
To put the Hub to work, start with one
clear request: create a venue visit

00:07:08.786 --> 00:07:11.974
checklist with preparation, on-site
checks, and follow-up actions.

00:07:11.974 --> 00:07:16.756
Review the draft, choose the audience, and
publish when it is ready.

00:07:16.756 --> 00:07:21.539
Resources, conversations, pages, and
access now live together in the ANC Hub.
